  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Text_note_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618129ca0c63c034993e09e51c102cb3, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 268590338048
    m_Localized: Was going home yesterday, some guy in a leather jacket and camo
      was standing on the platform staring at me the whole time. It was getting really
      uncomfortable. When the train came, he just stayed there. I switched cars.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 435724963840
    m_Localized: Saw that guy again today. Same station. Thought he might be following
      me but it's probably just a coincidence. People take the same train to work
      all the time. Still, he looks really weird.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 446806315008
    m_Localized: Very creepy guy.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 471959556096
    m_Localized: I don't know what's wrong with that guy but I really don't like
      being around him. He was standing by the stairs today and didn't even turn
      his head when I walked past. Somehow I still felt like he was watching me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 485167419392
    m_Localized: Saw him on the train today. Didn't recognize him at first, then
      realized it was the guy from the platform. There's something weird about his
      face, can't really explain it. Looks normal enough but I can't remember what
      he actually looks like.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 496009695232
    m_Localized: He was standing by the pillar this morning and was there again when
      I came back tonight. I even checked the time on my phone. No way someone would
      stand there all day. Maybe it's a different guy, but he's wearing the same
      clothes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 518344364032
    m_Localized: "he followed me all the way from my house!!! ALL THE WAY FROM MY
      HOUSE!!! I can\u2019t hear his steps at all, I\u2019m scared to look back,
      but I can feel him behind me. he went down into the metro with me. it\u2019s
      him, I know it\u2019s him"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 531308957696
    m_Localized: "I remembered where I\u2019ve seen him. In the paper, an article
      about a missing girl. He was standing in the crowd in the photo. I need to
      call the militia. If only I can get through."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 89359767298048
    m_Localized: "Today he got into my car. Sits across from me, hands on his knees,
      not moving. I\u2019m counting the stops. We\u2019ve been riding for too long,
      and there\u2019s no station."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5612847139643392
    m_Localized: Saw a guy with a knife near the station today. It was covered in
      blood, he put it away when he saw me. Called the police and they said they'd
      send someone. Been waiting for an hour, nobody showed up.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5612888407400448
    m_Localized: He was following me, I'm sure of it. First near my apartment, then
      on the street, then at the metro. I changed directions a few times on purpose
      and he was still around. When I got to the platform I looked back and saw him
      at the top of the stairs just looking down at me. Didn't wait for the train,
      left through another exit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5612932002996224
    m_Localized: Found an old newspaper article about a missing girl. That guy was
      standing in the crowd in one of the photos. Thought I was seeing things at
      first but zoomed in and he's definitely there. How did nobody notice him? The
      article says there were no witnesses.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5612966475980800
    m_Localized: He was on the train today. Didn't see him get on, just looked up
      and he was sitting across from me. Tried moving to another car but he was there
      too. Then the train stopped and the doors opened but there wasn't even a station.
      I should've been home ages ago. My phone has no signal.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
